A file with an unsupported extension (`.py`) is reported on stderr and makes the exit code 1, while the `.ts` file after it is still outlined.
== args
input/script.py
input/valid.ts
== file input/script.py
def hello():
    print("Hello")
== file input/valid.ts
function greet() {}
== stdout
input/valid.ts (1 line)
[L1-L1] function greet()
== stderr
File input/script.py has an unsupported file type; supported: .md, .ts, .mts, .cts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .rs, .css, .json, .toml, .yaml, .yml
== exit 1
